  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an integer NNN and a digit DDD. Find the minimum non-negetive integer you should add to NNN such that the final value of NNN does not contain the digit DDD.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line contains TTT denoting the number of test cases. Then the test cases follow.\nEach test case contains two integers NNN and DDD on a single line denoting the original number and the digit you need to avoid.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a single line the minimum non-negetive integer you should add to NNN.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤1091 \\leq N \\leq 10^91≤N≤109",
      "0≤D≤90 \\leq D \\leq 90≤D≤9",
      "Subtasks",
      "**Subtask 1 (100 points):** Original constraints"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "5\n21 5\n8 8\n100 0\n5925 9\n434356 3",
        "output": "0\n1\n11\n75\n5644",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: N=21N = 21N=21 does not contain the digit D=5D = 5D=5. Hence there is no need to add any integers to NNN.\nTest case 222: If 111 is added to N=8N = 8N=8, it becomes equal to 999, which does not contain the digit D=8D = 8D=8.\nTest case 333: The minimum integer you should add to N=100N = 100N=100 such that the final value of NNN does not contain the digit D=0D = 0D=0 is 111111.\nTest case 555: The minimum integer which is greater than 434356434356434356 and does not contain the digit D=3D = 3D=3 is 440000440000440000. So we should add 440000−434356=5644440000 - 434356 = 5644440000−434356=5644."
      }
    ]
  },
